  <!-- PHILOSOPHY -->
  <div class="callout">
    <div class="ctitle">📌 Philosophy &amp; Reading Order</div>
    <p>Every array algorithm in this volume is assembled from <b>8 core low-level code primitives</b>. The first <b>6 primitives</b> — introduced on the next page — cover pointer mechanics, swapping, in-place writes, running state, and guarded skipping. They carry Patterns 1–3 and the Guarded Skipping technique.</p>
    <p><b>Primitive 7 (window state expand/shrink)</b> is introduced immediately before Sliding Window. <b>Primitive 8 (cumulative state construction)</b> is introduced immediately before Prefix Sum. This keeps the reading order honest: you meet each primitive the moment the next pattern depends on it.</p>
  </div>

