  <!-- PRIMITIVES 1-6 -->
  <div class="page-break"></div>

  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Foundations</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge">The First 6 Primitives</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">Powers Patterns 1–3 and Guarded Skipping</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="prim">
    <div class="prim-head"><div class="prim-num">01</div><h4>Pointer &amp; Index Initialization</h4><span class="chip">O(1) time · O(1) space</span></div>
    <ul class="prim-list">
      <li><span class="k">Opposite Ends:</span> <code>left = 0</code> and <code>right = len(nums) - 1</code> — scan inward from both boundaries.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Same Direction:</span> <code>slow = 0</code> and <code>fast = 0</code> (or <code>1</code>) — filtering or cycle tracking.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Anchor &amp; Runner:</span> <code>left = 0</code> as anchor while <code>for right in range(n)</code> drives the runner.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Safety Bounds Guard:</span> Check <code>len(nums) == 0</code> or <code>len(nums) == 1</code> before accessing any index.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="prim">
    <div class="prim-head"><div class="prim-num">02</div><h4>Pointer Traversal &amp; Loop Bounds</h4><span class="chip">O(N) time · O(1) space</span></div>
    <ul class="prim-list">
      <li><span class="k">Strict Bound <code>while left &lt; right</code>:</span> Stops when <code>left == right</code>. Used for element pairs, swaps, and palindromes.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Inclusive Bound <code>while left &lt;= right</code>:</span> Processes the middle element when <code>left == right</code>.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Explicit Step Adjustments:</span> <code>left += 1</code>, <code>right -= 1</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="prim">
    <div class="prim-head"><div class="prim-num">03</div><h4>In-Place Swapping Mechanics</h4><span class="chip">O(1) per swap · O(1) space</span></div>
    <ul class="prim-list">
      <li><span class="k">Python Tuple Unpacking:</span> <code>nums[left], nums[right] = nums[right], nums[left]</code>.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Purpose:</span> Reorders elements directly inside existing memory without auxiliary buffers.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="prim">
    <div class="prim-head"><div class="prim-num">04</div><h4>Read &amp; Write Pointers (In-Place Overwriting)</h4><span class="chip">O(N) time · O(1) space</span></div>
    <ul class="prim-list">
      <li><span class="k">Dual Pointer Roles:</span> Read pointer scans every element; write pointer maintains the boundary of valid output.</li>
      <li><span class="k">The Overwrite Rule:</span> When <code>nums[read]</code> meets the criteria, execute <code>nums[write] = nums[read]</code> then <code>write += 1</code>.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Virtual Array Length:</span> The final value of <code>write</code> is the filtered subarray size.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="prim">
    <div class="prim-head"><div class="prim-num">05</div><h4>Extreme Values &amp; Running State Management</h4><span class="chip">O(1) per update · O(1) space</span></div>
    <ul class="prim-list">
      <li><span class="k">Initialization Standards:</span> <code>max_val = float('-inf')</code>, <code>min_val = float('inf')</code>, <code>running_sum = 0</code>.</li>
      <li><span class="k">State Updates:</span> Recompute each iteration, e.g. <code>max_val = max(max_val, candidate)</code>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="prim">
    <div class="prim-head"><div class="prim-num">06</div><h4>Guarded Skipping (Inner Loops)</h4><span class="chip">O(N) aggregate · O(1) space</span></div>
    <ul class="prim-list">
      <li><span class="k">Element Skipping:</span> Inner <code>while</code> loops advance over non-alphanumeric characters, spaces, or duplicate values.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Out-of-Bounds Protection Guard:</span> <b>Always</b> write <code>while left &lt; right and skip_condition:</code>.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Full chapter:</span> See the cross-cutting technique section in this volume.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- PATTERN 1 -->
  <div class="page-break"></div>
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Two Pointers Converging</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge">Pattern 1</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">Two bookmarks walking toward each other</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:13.8px;color:#475569;margin-bottom:22px;">
    Two pointers start at opposite ends of a sorted or symmetric data structure and step inward until they meet.
  </p>

  <!-- 1.1 -->
  <article class="example">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example 1.1</span><h3>Reverse String</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 344</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Reverse a string in-place using <b>O(1)</b> extra memory.</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force · O(N) time · O(N) space</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">def reverseString_brute_force(s: list[str]) -&gt; None:
    temp = s[::-1]              <span class="cm"># O(N) auxiliary space</span>
    for i in range(len(s)):
        s[i] = temp[i]</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Two Pointers · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code"><span class="cm"># Primitive 1: Opposite ends initialization</span>
left = 0
right = len(s) - 1

<span class="cm"># Primitive 2: Strict bound loop (stops when left == right)</span>
while left &lt; right:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 3: In-place tuple swap</span>
    s[left], s[right] = s[right], s[left]
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: Explicit pointer movement</span>
    left += 1
    right -= 1</pre>
    <div class="subhead fc"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Reverse String — Swap Inward</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 320" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Reverse String — Swap Inward">
        <rect x="250.8" y="10" width="158.4" height="34" rx="9" fill="#0f2a4a"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">L = 0, R = n − 1</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <polygon points="330,72 450,106 330,140 210,106" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">L &lt; R ?</text>
        <path d="M330 140 L330 168" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="158" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#2563eb">Yes</text>
        <path d="M450 106 L500 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="500" y="88" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">End</text>
        <rect x="245" y="168" width="170" height="36" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="190" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">swap s[L] ↔ s[R]</text>
        <path d="M330 204 L330 232" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="245" y="232" width="170" height="36" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="254" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">L++ , R−−</text>
        <path d="M330 268 L330 298" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M330 298 L10 298 L10 106 L210 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="viz-label">Final · <code>left == right</code> → loop terminates</div>
    <div class="viz">
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">o</div><div class="idx">0</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">l</div><div class="idx">1</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"><span class="ptr meet">L·R</span></div><div class="cell a">l</div><div class="idx">2</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">e</div><div class="idx">3</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">h</div><div class="idx">4</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="result-pill">Final Result: ['o','l','l','e','h']</div>
  </article>

  <!-- 1.2 -->
  <article class="example">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example 1.2</span><h3>Two Sum II — Input Array Is Sorted</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 167</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Find two numbers in a 1-indexed sorted array that sum to a target. Return their 1-indexed positions.</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force · O(N²) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">def twoSum_brute_force(numbers: list[int], target: int) -&gt; list[int]:
    n = len(numbers)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(i + 1, n):
            if numbers[i] + numbers[j] == target:
                return [i + 1, j + 1]
    return []</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Two Pointers · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code"><span class="cm"># Primitive 1: Opposite ends initialization</span>
left = 0
right = len(numbers) - 1

<span class="cm"># Primitive 2: Strict bound convergence loop</span>
while left &lt; right:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Calculate running sum state</span>
    current_sum = numbers[left] + numbers[right]

    if current_sum == target:
        return [left + 1, right + 1]
    elif current_sum &lt; target:
        left += 1
    else:
        right -= 1
return []</pre>
    <div class="subhead fc"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Two Sum II — Meet in the Middle</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 448" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Two Sum II — Meet in the Middle">
        <rect x="250.8" y="10" width="158.4" height="34" rx="9" fill="#0f2a4a"/>
