  <!-- PATTERN 5 -->
  <div class="page-break"></div>
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Two-Array Merge</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge badge-purple">Pattern 5</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">One pointer per input — advance whichever is behind</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:13.8px;color:#475569;margin-bottom:22px;">
    Unlike converging (which uses two pointers on <b>one</b> array), two-array merge uses <b>one pointer on each of two inputs</b>. The two pointers never meet — they walk independently, and the algorithm ends when either input is exhausted. This is the pattern behind every merge operation, intersection, and subsequence check.
  </p>

  <!-- 5.1 -->
  <article class="example purple">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example 5.1</span><h3>Is Subsequence</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 392</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Given strings <code>s</code> and <code>t</code>, return true if <code>s</code> is a subsequence of <code>t</code> (i.e., <code>s</code> can be formed by deleting characters from <code>t</code> without reordering).</p>

    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force · O(2^N) time · O(2^N) space</div>
    <p class="bf-note">Generate all subsequences of <code>t</code>, check if <code>s</code> is one of them. <b>Exponential — impractical.</b></p>

<pre class="code bf-code">def isSubsequence_brute_force(s: str, t: str) -&gt; bool:
    def all_subsequences(x):
        if not x:
            return {""}
        rest = all_subsequences(x[1:])
        return rest | {x[0] + sub for sub in rest}
    return s in all_subsequences(t)</pre>

    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Two-Array Merge · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>

<pre class="code purple-code">def isSubsequence(s: str, t: str) -&gt; bool:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 1: One pointer per input, both at the start</span>
    i = 0
    j = 0

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: Loop until either input is exhausted</span>
    while i &lt; len(s) and j &lt; len(t):
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Compare the current pair of characters</span>
        if s[i] == t[j]:
            <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: Match — advance both pointers</span>
            i += 1
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: Always advance the t pointer</span>
        j += 1

    <span class="cm"># s is a subsequence iff we consumed all of s</span>
    return i == len(s)</pre>

    <div class="subhead fc-purple"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Is Subsequence — Advance Both on Match</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 352" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Is Subsequence — Advance Both on Match">
        <rect x="255" y="10" width="150" height="34" rx="9" fill="#7c3aed"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">i = 0, j = 0</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <polygon points="330,72 450,106 330,140 210,106" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">i &lt; len(s)</text>
        <text x="330" y="118" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">AND j &lt; len(t) ?</text>
        <path d="M330 140 L330 168" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="158" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#7c3aed">Yes</text>
        <path d="M450 106 L500 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="500" y="83" width="130" height="46" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="102" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return</text>
        <text x="565" y="118" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">i == len(s)</text>
        <polygon points="330,168 450,202 330,236 210,202" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="206" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">s[i] == t[j] ?</text>
        <path d="M330 236 L330 264" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="254" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <path d="M210 202 L160 202" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="185" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#7c3aed">Yes</text>
        <rect x="30" y="184" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#c4b5fd" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="95" y="206" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#6b21a8" font-family="monospace">i++</text>
        <path d="M95 220 L95 250 L330 250" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <rect x="245" y="264" width="170" height="36" rx="9" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#c4b5fd" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="286" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#6b21a8" font-family="monospace">j++</text>
        <path d="M330 300 L330 330" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M330 330 L10 330 L10 106 L210 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="viz-label">Step 3 · <code>s = "ace"</code>, <code>t = "abcde"</code> · i and j both point at 'c' → match, advance both</div>
