  <!-- PRIMITIVE 8 + PATTERN 6 -->
  <div class="page-break"></div>
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Foundations · The Eighth Primitive</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge badge-indigo">Primitive 8</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">Introduced here because Prefix Sum depends on it</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:13.8px;color:#475569;margin-bottom:22px;">
    Every primitive so far works on <b>the current element</b>. Prefix Sum needs something different: a <b>precomputed array</b> whose values are cumulative sums, so that range queries answer in O(1) instead of O(k). This is the first primitive that builds a data structure, not a pointer.
  </p>

  <div class="prim new-indigo">
    <div class="prim-head"><div class="prim-num">08</div><h4>Cumulative State Construction (Prefix Sum / Product)</h4><span class="chip new-chip-indigo">O(N) build · O(1) query · O(N) space</span></div>
    <ul class="prim-list">
      <li><span class="k">Prefix Array Build:</span> <code>prefix[i] = prefix[i-1] + nums[i-1]</code>, with a leading <code>prefix[0] = 0</code>. The extra leading slot eliminates all "what if left == 0" edge cases.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Range Sum Query:</span> <code>range_sum(l, r) = prefix[r+1] - prefix[l]</code> — O(1) regardless of window size.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Prefix Products:</span> Same shape with multiplicative identity <code>1</code> instead of <code>0</code>. Breaks if the array contains a 0 (you cannot divide by it), which is why Example 6.3 avoids division entirely. Often paired with a mirrored <b>suffix</b> array to answer "everything except index i" queries.</li>
      <li><span class="k">Prefix + Suffix Pairs:</span> Build both arrays in one pass each; the answer at index <code>i</code> combines <code>prefix[i]</code> and <code>suffix[i+1]</code>.</li>
      <li><span class="k">The Invariant:</span> <code>prefix[i]</code> equals the sum (or product) of <code>nums[0..i-1]</code>. Never includes index <code>i</code> itself.</li>
      <li><span class="k">What it does NOT do:</span> Prefix sum only works when the operation is <b>invertible</b> (sum, XOR; product only while no element is 0). It does not handle min/max queries — those need a monotonic deque (Volume 3) or a sparse table / segment tree (Volume 4). If the array changes between queries, use a Fenwick tree (Volume 4).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:34px;">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Prefix Sum</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge badge-indigo">Pattern 6</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">Trade O(N) build for O(1) range queries</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 6.1 -->
  <article class="example indigo">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example 6.1</span><h3>Range Sum Query — Immutable</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 303</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Design a class that answers many <code>sumRange(left, right)</code> queries on a static array. Each query must be O(1).</p>

    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force · O(N) per query · O(1) space</div>
    <p class="bf-note">Recompute the sum for every query by iterating <code>nums[left..right]</code>. <b>Too slow when queries are frequent.</b></p>

<pre class="code bf-code">class NumArray_brute_force:
    def __init__(self, nums: list[int]):
        self.nums = nums

    def sumRange(self, left: int, right: int) -&gt; int:
        return sum(self.nums[left:right+1])    <span class="cm"># O(N) per query</span></pre>

    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Precomputed Prefix Sum · O(N) build · O(1) per query</div>

<pre class="code indigo-code">class NumArray:
    def __init__(self, nums: list[int]):
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: Build prefix array with a leading 0</span>
        self.prefix = [0] * (len(nums) + 1)
        for i in range(len(nums)):
            <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: Cumulative state construction</span>
            self.prefix[i + 1] = self.prefix[i] + nums[i]

    def sumRange(self, left: int, right: int) -&gt; int:
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: O(1) range query via prefix difference</span>
        return self.prefix[right + 1] - self.prefix[left]</pre>

    <div class="subhead fc-indigo"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Range Sum — Build Once, Query in O(1)</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 500 300" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <rect x="160" y="10" width="180" height="36" rx="9" fill="#4338ca"/>
        <text x="250" y="33" fill="#fff" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">__init__: build prefix</text>
        <line x1="250" y1="46" x2="250" y2="72" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#arI)"/>
        <rect x="100" y="72" width="300" height="42" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="250" y="93" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">prefix[0] = 0</text>
        <text x="250" y="108" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">prefix[i+1] = prefix[i] + nums[i]</text>
        <line x1="250" y1="114" x2="250" y2="148" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#arI)"/>
        <rect x="130" y="148" width="240" height="46" rx="9" fill="#4338ca"/>
        <text x="250" y="172" fill="#fff" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">sumRange(l, r) — O(1)</text>
        <text x="250" y="186" fill="#fff" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace">prefix[r+1] − prefix[l]</text>
        <line x1="250" y1="194" x2="250" y2="224" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#arI)"/>
        <rect x="140" y="224" width="220" height="40" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <text x="250" y="249" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return range sum</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="viz-label">Prefix array for <code>nums = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]</code> · query <code>sumRange(1, 3) = prefix[4] − prefix[1] = 9 − 3 = 6</code></div>
    <div class="viz wrap">
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"><span class="ptr indigo">p</span></div><div class="cell i">0</div><div class="idx">0</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">3</div><div class="idx">1</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">4</div><div class="idx">2</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">8</div><div class="idx">3</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">9</div><div class="idx">4</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">14</div><div class="idx">5</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="result-pill">Query <code>sumRange(1, 3)</code> on <code>[3,1,4,1,5]</code>: 6</div>
  </article>

  <!-- 6.2 -->
  <article class="example indigo">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example 6.2</span><h3>Find Pivot Index</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 724</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Return the leftmost index where the sum of elements strictly to the left equals the sum strictly to the right. Return −1 if none.</p>

    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force · O(N²) time · O(1) space</div>
    <p class="bf-note">For each index, recompute left and right sums. <b>Quadratic on large inputs.</b></p>

<pre class="code bf-code">def pivotIndex_brute_force(nums: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    for i in range(len(nums)):
        if sum(nums[:i]) == sum(nums[i+1:]):
            return i
    return -1</pre>

    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Total Sum + Running Left · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>

<pre class="code indigo-code">def pivotIndex(nums: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: Total sum — the prefix of the whole array, computed once</span>
    total = sum(nums)

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Running left-sum state</span>
    left_sum = 0

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: Single forward pass</span>
    for i in range(len(nums)):
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: Right sum = total − left_sum − nums[i]</span>
        if left_sum == total - left_sum - nums[i]:
            return i
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Extend the running left-sum state</span>
        left_sum += nums[i]

    return -1</pre>

    <div class="subhead fc-indigo"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Find Pivot Index — Running Left vs. Implied Right</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 352" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Find Pivot Index — Running Left vs. Implied Right">
        <rect x="210.1" y="10" width="239.8" height="34" rx="9" fill="#4338ca"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">total = sum(nums); left = 0</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <polygon points="330,72 450,106 330,140 210,106" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">i &lt; n ?</text>
        <path d="M330 140 L330 168" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="158" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#4338ca">Yes</text>
        <path d="M450 106 L500 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="500" y="88" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#f1f5f9" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#475569">return −1</text>
        <polygon points="330,168 458,202 330,236 202,202" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="198" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">left == total −</text>
        <text x="330" y="214" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">left − nums[i] ?</text>
        <path d="M330 236 L330 264" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="254" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <path d="M202 202 L152 202" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="177" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#4338ca">Yes</text>
        <rect x="22" y="184" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="87" y="206" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return i</text>
        <rect x="245" y="264" width="170" height="36" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="286" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">left += nums[i]</text>
        <path d="M330 300 L330 330" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M330 330 L10 330 L10 106 L210 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>[1,7,3,6,5,6]</code>: 3</div>
  </article>

  <!-- 6.3 -->
  <article class="example indigo">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example 6.3</span><h3>Product of Array Except Self</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 238</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Return an array <code>output</code> where <code>output[i]</code> is the product of all elements of <code>nums</code> except <code>nums[i]</code>. Solve in O(N) time and O(1) extra space (output array does not count).</p>

    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force · O(N²) time · O(1) extra space</div>
    <p class="bf-note">For each <code>i</code>, compute the product of all other elements. <b>Divisions are banned by the problem constraints.</b></p>

<pre class="code bf-code">def productExceptSelf_brute_force(nums: list[int]) -&gt; list[int]:
    n = len(nums)
    res = [1] * n
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(n):
            if i != j:
                res[i] *= nums[j]
    return res</pre>

    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Prefix × Suffix (in place) · O(N) time · O(1) extra space</div>

<pre class="code indigo-code">def productExceptSelf(nums: list[int]) -&gt; list[int]:
    n = len(nums)
    res = [1] * n

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: Prefix pass — res[i] = product of nums[0..i-1]</span>
    prefix = 1
    for i in range(n):
        res[i] = prefix
        prefix *= nums[i]

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: Suffix pass — multiply in product of nums[i+1..n-1]</span>
    suffix = 1
    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):
        res[i] *= suffix
        suffix *= nums[i]

    return res</pre>

    <div class="subhead fc-indigo"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Product Except Self — Prefix Pass, Then Suffix Pass</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 500 380" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <rect x="150" y="10" width="200" height="36" rx="9" fill="#4338ca"/>
        <text x="250" y="33" fill="#fff" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">prefix = 1; res = [1]*n</text>
        <line x1="250" y1="46" x2="250" y2="72" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#arI)"/>
        <rect x="130" y="72" width="240" height="42" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="250" y="93" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81">Forward pass (i →)</text>
        <text x="250" y="108" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">res[i] = prefix; prefix *= nums[i]</text>
        <line x1="250" y1="114" x2="250" y2="140" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#arI)"/>
        <rect x="130" y="140" width="240" height="42" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="250" y="161" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81">Backward pass (← i)</text>
        <text x="250" y="176" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">res[i] *= suffix; suffix *= nums[i]</text>
        <line x1="250" y1="182" x2="250" y2="214" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#arI)"/>
        <rect x="160" y="214" width="180" height="40" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <text x="250" y="239" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return res</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="viz-label">After both passes · <code>nums = [1,2,3,4]</code> → <code>res = [24,12,8,6]</code></div>
    <div class="viz">
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"><span class="ptr indigo">p→</span></div><div class="cell i">1</div><div class="idx">0</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">2</div><div class="idx">1</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"><span class="ptr indigo">←s</span></div><div class="cell i">3</div><div class="idx">2</div></div>
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">4</div><div class="idx">3</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>[1,2,3,4]</code>: [24, 12, 8, 6]</div>
  </article>

  <!-- PATTERN 7 KADANE -->
  <div class="page-break"></div>
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Kadane / Running Extremes</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge badge-purple">Pattern 7</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">No pointers — just running state</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:13.8px;color:#475569;margin-bottom:22px;">
    Kadane shows that a real algorithm can be built with <b>no pointers at all</b>. It needs only Primitive 5 (extreme values and running state) plus a plain forward loop (Primitive 2). The insight is that for many problems, the "best ending at <code>i</code>" can be computed from the "best ending at <code>i-1</code>" with a single comparison. The whole algorithm is a state update.
  </p>

  <!-- 7.1 -->
  <article class="example purple">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example 7.1</span><h3>Maximum Subarray</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 53</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Find the contiguous subarray with the largest sum. Return that sum.</p>

    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force · O(N²) time · O(1) space</div>
    <p class="bf-note">Try every starting index and extend. <b>Quadratic on large inputs.</b></p>

<pre class="code bf-code">def maxSubArray_brute_force(nums: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    n = len(nums)
    best = float('-inf')
    for i in range(n):
        running = 0
        for j in range(i, n):
            running += nums[j]
            best = max(best, running)
    return best</pre>

    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Kadane's · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>

<pre class="code purple-code">def maxSubArray(nums: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Two running states — best ending here, best overall</span>
    <span class="cm"># LeetCode guarantees len(nums) &gt;= 1; in your own code add the Primitive 1 guard first</span>
    best_ending_here = nums[0]
    best_overall = nums[0]

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: Single forward pass (loop only, no pointer)</span>
    for i in range(1, len(nums)):
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Extend the previous run, or start fresh at nums[i]</span>
        best_ending_here = max(nums[i], best_ending_here + nums[i])
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Update the global best</span>
        best_overall = max(best_overall, best_ending_here)

    return best_overall</pre>

    <div class="subhead fc-purple"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Maximum Subarray — Extend or Restart</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 320" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Maximum Subarray — Extend or Restart">
        <rect x="199" y="10" width="262" height="34" rx="9" fill="#7c3aed"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">here = nums[0]; best = nums[0]</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <polygon points="330,72 450,106 330,140 210,106" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">i &lt; n ?</text>
        <path d="M330 140 L330 168" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="158" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#7c3aed">Yes</text>
        <path d="M450 106 L500 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="500" y="88" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return best</text>
        <rect x="189.25" y="168" width="281.5" height="36" rx="9" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#c4b5fd" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="190" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#6b21a8" font-family="monospace">here = max(nums[i], here + nums[i])</text>
        <path d="M330 204 L330 232" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="234.1" y="232" width="191.8" height="36" rx="9" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#c4b5fd" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="254" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#6b21a8" font-family="monospace">best = max(best, here)</text>
        <path d="M330 268 L330 298" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M330 298 L10 298 L10 106 L210 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="viz-label">At i = 3 · <code>nums = [-2,1,-3,4,-1,2,1,-5,4]</code> · here = 4, best = 4</div>
    <div class="viz wrap">
      <div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">−2</div><div class="idx">0</div></div>
