  </article>

  <!-- 7.2 -->
  <article class="example purple">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example 7.2</span><h3>Maximum Product Subarray</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 152</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Find the contiguous subarray with the largest product.</p>

    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force · O(N²) time · O(1) space</div>
    <p class="bf-note">Try every subarray and take the product. <b>Quadratic.</b></p>

<pre class="code bf-code">def maxProduct_brute_force(nums: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    n = len(nums)
    best = float('-inf')
    for i in range(n):
        running = 1
        for j in range(i, n):
            running *= nums[j]
            best = max(best, running)
    return best</pre>

    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Kadane with Min/Max Pair · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>

<pre class="code purple-code">def maxProduct(nums: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Track BOTH running max and running min (negatives flip signs)</span>
    <span class="cm"># LeetCode guarantees len(nums) &gt;= 1; in your own code add the Primitive 1 guard first</span>
    cur_max = nums[0]
    cur_min = nums[0]
    best = nums[0]

    for i in range(1, len(nums)):
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Compute both candidates before overwriting either</span>
        candidates = (nums[i], cur_max * nums[i], cur_min * nums[i])
        cur_max = max(candidates)
        cur_min = min(candidates)
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 5: Update global best using the running max</span>
        best = max(best, cur_max)

    return best</pre>

    <div class="subhead fc-purple"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Maximum Product Subarray — Track Min and Max</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 398" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Maximum Product Subarray — Track Min and Max">
        <rect x="147.2" y="10" width="365.6" height="34" rx="9" fill="#7c3aed"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">max = nums[0], min = nums[0], best = nums[0]</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <polygon points="330,72 450,106 330,140 210,106" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">i &lt; n ?</text>
        <path d="M330 140 L330 168" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="158" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#7c3aed">Yes</text>
        <path d="M450 106 L500 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="500" y="88" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return best</text>
        <rect x="161.65" y="168" width="336.7" height="50" rx="9" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#c4b5fd" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="190" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#6b21a8" font-family="monospace">cands = (nums[i], max*nums[i], min*nums[i])</text>
        <text x="330" y="210" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#6b21a8" font-style="italic">negatives swap max and min — evaluate both first</text>
        <path d="M330 218 L330 246" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="192.7" y="246" width="274.6" height="36" rx="9" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#c4b5fd" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="268" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#6b21a8" font-family="monospace">max = max(cands); min = min(cands)</text>
        <path d="M330 282 L330 310" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="237.55" y="310" width="184.9" height="36" rx="9" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#c4b5fd" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="332" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#6b21a8" font-family="monospace">best = max(best, max)</text>
        <path d="M330 346 L330 376" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M330 376 L10 376 L10 106 L210 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>[2,3,-2,4]</code>: 6 → [2, 3]</div>
  </article>

  <!-- EXTENSIONS -->
  <div class="page-break"></div>
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Extensions</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge badge-rose">Filling the Gaps</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">Variants and capstones that reuse Patterns 1–7</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="font-size:13.8px;color:#475569;margin-bottom:22px;">
    Eight more problems that interviews love. Each one is a <b>variation</b> of a pattern you already know: three pointers instead of two, pointers moving <i>outward</i>, a window that counts instead of tracks, or a prefix sum that needs a hash map. Same primitives, one new twist each.
  </p>

  <article class="example">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example X.1</span><h3>Sort Colors (Dutch National Flag)</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 75</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Sort an array containing only <code>0</code>, <code>1</code> and <code>2</code> <b>in place</b> in a single pass, without calling <code>sort</code>.</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force — Count, Then Overwrite · O(N) time · O(1) space (two passes)</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">def sortColors_two_pass(nums: list[int]) -&gt; None:
    <span class="cm"># Count each color, then overwrite the array in order</span>
    counts = [0, 0, 0]
    for x in nums:
        counts[x] += 1
    write = 0
    for color in range(3):
        for _ in range(counts[color]):
            nums[write] = color
            write += 1</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Three Pointers, One Pass · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code ">def sortColors(nums: list[int]) -&gt; None:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 1: low = next slot for 0s, high = next slot for 2s, mid = scanner</span>
    low, mid, high = 0, 0, len(nums) - 1

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: INCLUSIVE bound - nums[mid] == nums[high] is still unchecked</span>
    while mid &lt;= high:
        if nums[mid] == 0:
            <span class="cm"># Primitive 3: swap a 0 into the front zone</span>
            nums[low], nums[mid] = nums[mid], nums[low]
            low += 1
            mid += 1        <span class="cm"># safe: whatever came from low is already a 1</span>
        elif nums[mid] == 1:
            mid += 1
        else:
            <span class="cm"># Primitive 3: swap a 2 into the back zone</span>
            nums[mid], nums[high] = nums[high], nums[mid]
            high -= 1       <span class="cm"># do NOT advance mid: the swapped-in value is unchecked</span></pre>
    <p class="bf-note"><b>Invariant:</b> <code>[0, low)</code> are 0s · <code>[low, mid)</code> are 1s · <code>[mid, high]</code> is still unknown · <code>(high, n)</code> are 2s. This extends Pattern 2: the write position is split into <i>two</i> zones.</p>
    <div class="subhead fc"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Sort Colors — Dutch National Flag</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 476" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Sort Colors — Dutch National Flag">
        <rect x="199" y="10" width="262" height="34" rx="9" fill="#0f2a4a"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">low = 0, mid = 0, high = n − 1</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <polygon points="330,72 450,106 330,140 210,106" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">mid ≤ high ?</text>
        <path d="M330 140 L330 168" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="158" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#2563eb">Yes</text>
        <path d="M450 106 L500 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="500" y="88" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">End</text>
        <polygon points="330,168 450,202 330,236 210,202" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="206" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">nums[mid] == 0 ?</text>
        <path d="M330 236 L330 264" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="254" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <path d="M450 202 L500 202" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#2563eb">Yes</text>
        <rect x="500" y="179" width="130" height="46" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="198" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">swap low ↔ mid</text>
        <text x="565" y="214" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">low++, mid++</text>
        <polygon points="330,264 450,298 330,332 210,298" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="302" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">nums[mid] == 1 ?</text>
        <path d="M330 332 L330 360" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="350" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <path d="M210 298 L160 298" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="185" y="292" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#2563eb">Yes</text>
        <rect x="30" y="280" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="95" y="302" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">mid++</text>
        <rect x="245" y="360" width="170" height="46" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="379" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">swap mid ↔ high</text>
        <text x="330" y="395" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">high−−</text>
        <path d="M330 406 L330 436" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M565 225 L565 436" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M95 316 L95 436" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M565 436 L10 436 L10 106 L210 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="330" y="462" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="500" fill="#475569" font-style="italic">After swapping with high, do NOT advance mid — the new value is unchecked.</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="viz-label">Snapshot after 4 steps · <code>[2,0,2,1,1,0]</code> → <code>low = mid = 2, high = 3</code></div>
<div class="viz"><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">0</div><div class="idx">0</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">0</div><div class="idx">1</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"><span class="ptr purple">L·M</span></div><div class="cell i">1</div><div class="idx">2</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"><span class="ptr amber">H</span></div><div class="cell i">1</div><div class="idx">3</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">2</div><div class="idx">4</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell done">2</div><div class="idx">5</div></div></div>
    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>[2,0,2,1,1,0]</code>: [0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]</div>
  </article>

  <article class="example">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example X.2</span><h3>Longest Palindromic Substring</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 5 · 647</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Return the longest palindromic substring of <code>s</code>. (LeetCode 647 counts all palindromic substrings using the same idea.)</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force — Check Every Substring · O(N³) time · O(N) space</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">def longestPalindrome_brute_force(s: str) -&gt; str:
    best = ""
    for i in range(len(s)):
        for j in range(i, len(s)):
            sub = s[i:j + 1]
            if sub == sub[::-1] and len(sub) &gt; len(best):
                best = sub
    return best</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Expand Around Center · O(N²) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code ">def longestPalindrome(s: str) -&gt; str:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 1: remember the best window as two indices (no substring copies)</span>
    best_l, best_r = 0, 0

    def expand(l: int, r: int) -&gt; tuple[int, int]:
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 2 + Guard: check bounds BEFORE comparing characters</span>
        while l &gt;= 0 and r &lt; len(s) and s[l] == s[r]:
            <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: pointers move OUTWARD (mirror image of Pattern 1)</span>
            l -= 1
            r += 1
        return l + 1, r - 1     <span class="cm"># last window that was still a palindrome</span>

    for i in range(len(s)):
        <span class="cm"># Odd-length centers sit on i; even-length centers sit between i and i+1</span>
        for l, r in (expand(i, i), expand(i, i + 1)):
            if r - l &gt; best_r - best_l:
                best_l, best_r = l, r
    return s[best_l:best_r + 1]</pre>
    <p class="bf-note"><b>Why 2N − 1 centers:</b> every palindrome mirrors around one character (odd length) or one gap between two characters (even length). <b>Mirror of Pattern 1:</b> Converging shrinks toward a meeting point; this pattern <i>grows away</i> from one. (An O(N) version exists — Manacher's algorithm — but is beyond this series.)</p>
<pre class="code ">def countSubstrings(s: str) -&gt; int:      <span class="cm"># LeetCode 647: same idea, count instead of track best</span>
    count = 0
    for center in range(2 * len(s) - 1):
        l = center // 2
        r = l + center % 2
        while l &gt;= 0 and r &lt; len(s) and s[l] == s[r]:
            count += 1                    <span class="cm"># every successful expansion is one palindrome</span>
            l -= 1
            r += 1
    return count</pre>
    <div class="subhead fc"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Longest Palindromic Substring — Expand Around Center</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 456" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Longest Palindromic Substring — Expand Around Center">
        <rect x="255" y="10" width="150" height="34" rx="9" fill="#0f2a4a"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">best = (0, 0)</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="210" y="72" width="240" height="44" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="91" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a">for i in range(n):</text>
        <text x="330" y="107" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="500" fill="#0f2a4a">try center (i, i) and (i, i+1)</text>
        <path d="M330 116 L330 144" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <path d="M450 94 L500 94" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#2563eb">done</text>
