    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>"babad"</code>: "bab" (<code>"aba"</code> is equally valid)</div>
  </article>

  <article class="example indigo">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example X.3</span><h3>Trapping Rain Water</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 42</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Given <code>n</code> bar heights, compute how much rain water is trapped between the bars. A capstone that combines <b>Pattern 1</b> (converging) with <b>Primitive 8</b> (prefix/suffix maxima).</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force — Look Both Ways for Every Bar · O(N²) time · O(N) space</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">def trap_brute_force(height: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    water = 0
    for i in range(len(height)):
        left_max = max(height[:i + 1])      <span class="cm"># tallest bar at or left of i</span>
        right_max = max(height[i:])         <span class="cm"># tallest bar at or right of i</span>
        water += min(left_max, right_max) - height[i]
    return water</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Middle Step — Prefix / Suffix Max Arrays · O(N) time · O(N) space</div>
<pre class="code indigo-code">def trap_prefix_suffix(height: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    n = len(height)
    if n == 0:
        return 0
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: prefix-max and suffix-max arrays</span>
    left_max = [0] * n
    right_max = [0] * n
    left_max[0] = height[0]
    for i in range(1, n):
        left_max[i] = max(left_max[i - 1], height[i])
    right_max[n - 1] = height[n - 1]
    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):
        right_max[i] = max(right_max[i + 1], height[i])
    return sum(min(left_max[i], right_max[i]) - height[i] for i in range(n))</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Converging with Running Maxima · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code indigo-code">def trap(height: list[int]) -&gt; int:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 1 + Guard: empty input</span>
    if not height:
        return 0

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 1 + 5: opposite ends, plus a running max on each side</span>
    left, right = 0, len(height) - 1
    left_max = right_max = 0
    water = 0

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: strict bound - stop when the pointers meet</span>
    while left &lt; right:
        <span class="cm"># The SHORTER side is the bottleneck, so its water level is already known</span>
        if height[left] &lt; height[right]:
            left_max = max(left_max, height[left])
            water += left_max - height[left]
            left += 1
        else:
            right_max = max(right_max, height[right])
            water += right_max - height[right]
            right -= 1
    return water</pre>
    <p class="bf-note"><b>Why moving the shorter side is safe:</b> water above a bar = <code>min(tallest to its left, tallest to its right) − height</code>. If <code>height[left] &lt; height[right]</code>, the right side already guarantees a wall at least that tall, so <code>left_max</code> alone decides the level at <code>left</code>.</p>
    <div class="subhead fc-indigo"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Trapping Rain Water — Shorter Side Moves</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 293.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Trapping Rain Water — Shorter Side Moves">
        <rect x="210.1" y="10" width="239.8" height="34" rx="9" fill="#4338ca"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">L = 0, R = n − 1, water = 0</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <polygon points="330,72 450,106 330,140 210,106" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">L &lt; R ?</text>
        <path d="M330 140 L330 168" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="158" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#4338ca">Yes</text>
        <path d="M450 106 L500 106" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="500" y="88" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return water</text>
        <polygon points="330,168 450,202 330,236 210,202" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="206" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">h[L] &lt; h[R] ?</text>
        <path d="M210 202 L160 202" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="185" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#4338ca">Yes</text>
        <rect x="30" y="163" width="130" height="78" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="95" y="182" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">update left_max</text>
        <text x="95" y="198" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">water += left_max</text>
        <text x="95" y="214" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">− h[L]</text>
        <text x="95" y="230" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">L++</text>
        <path d="M450 202 L500 202" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="196" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="500" y="163" width="130" height="78" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="182" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">update right_max</text>
        <text x="565" y="198" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">water += right_max</text>
        <text x="565" y="214" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">− h[R]</text>
        <text x="565" y="230" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">R−−</text>
