    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>[0,1,0,2,1,0,1,3,2,1,2,1]</code>: 6</div>
  </article>

  <article class="example teal">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example X.4</span><h3>Longest Repeating Character Replacement</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 424</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">You may replace at most <code>k</code> characters of <code>s</code> with any letter. Return the length of the longest substring that can become one repeated letter.</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force — Try Every Substring · O(N³) time · O(1) space (26 letters)</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">from collections import Counter

def characterReplacement_brute_force(s: str, k: int) -&gt; int:
    best = 0
    for i in range(len(s)):
        for j in range(i, len(s)):
            window = s[i:j + 1]
            <span class="cm"># replacements needed = window size - count of its most common letter</span>
            if len(window) - max(Counter(window).values()) &lt;= k:
                best = max(best, len(window))
    return best</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Window That Needs ≤ k Edits · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code teal-code">def characterReplacement(s: str, k: int) -&gt; int:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 1 + 5: window start, letter counts, best frequency seen so far</span>
    counts = {}
    left = 0
    max_freq = 0
    best = 0

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 2: right pointer expands the window</span>
    for right, ch in enumerate(s):
        counts[ch] = counts.get(ch, 0) + 1
        max_freq = max(max_freq, counts[ch])

        <span class="cm"># Primitive 7: shrink while the replacements needed exceed k</span>
        <span class="cm"># replacements needed = window size - most frequent letter</span>
        while (right - left + 1) - max_freq &gt; k:
            counts[s[left]] -= 1
            left += 1

        best = max(best, right - left + 1)
    return best</pre>
    <p class="bf-note"><b>The stale-max trick:</b> <code>max_freq</code> is never lowered when the window shrinks. That is safe, because the answer only grows when a <i>new, higher</i> frequency appears, so an outdated value can never produce a wrongly large window.</p>
    <div class="subhead fc-teal"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Longest Repeating Character Replacement — Window Needing ≤ k Edits</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 328" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Longest Repeating Character Replacement — Window Needing ≤ k Edits">
        <rect x="143.5" y="10" width="373" height="34" rx="9" fill="#0891b2"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">left = 0, counts = {}, max_freq = 0, best = 0</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="210" y="72" width="240" height="44" rx="9" fill="#cffafe" stroke="#67e8f9" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="91" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#155e75">for right in range(n):</text>
        <text x="330" y="107" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="500" fill="#155e75">add s[right]; update max_freq</text>
        <path d="M330 116 L330 144" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <path d="M450 94 L500 94" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0891b2">done</text>
        <rect x="500" y="76" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="98" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return best</text>
        <polygon points="330,144 450,178 330,212 210,178" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="174" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">window size</text>
        <text x="330" y="190" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">− max_freq &gt; k ?</text>
        <path d="M330 212 L330 240" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="230" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <path d="M210 178 L160 178" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="185" y="172" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0891b2">Yes</text>
        <rect x="30" y="155" width="130" height="46" rx="9" fill="#cffafe" stroke="#67e8f9" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="95" y="174" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-weight="800" fill="#155e75" font-family="monospace">counts[s[left]] −= 1</text>
        <text x="95" y="190" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" font-weight="800" fill="#155e75" font-family="monospace">left++</text>
        <path d="M95 155 L95 130 L330 130" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <rect x="206.5" y="240" width="247" height="36" rx="9" fill="#cffafe" stroke="#67e8f9" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="262" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#155e75" font-family="monospace">best = max(best, right−left+1)</text>
        <path d="M330 276 L330 306" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M330 306 L10 306 L10 94 L210 94" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>s = "AABABBA", k = 1</code>: 4</div>
  </article>

  <article class="example teal">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example X.5</span><h3>At Most K Distinct — and the “Exactly K” Trick</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 340 / 904 · 992</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">(a) Longest substring with <b>at most k</b> distinct characters. (b) Count subarrays with <b>exactly k</b> distinct integers. Part (b) cannot be solved by a single window, but it falls out of part (a).</p>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Window + Frequency Map · O(N) time · O(k) space</div>
<pre class="code teal-code">def longestAtMostKDistinct(s: str, k: int) -&gt; int:
    counts = {}
    left = 0
    best = 0
    for right, ch in enumerate(s):
        counts[ch] = counts.get(ch, 0) + 1
        <span class="cm"># Primitive 7: shrink until at most k distinct letters remain</span>
        while len(counts) &gt; k:
            counts[s[left]] -= 1
            if counts[s[left]] == 0:
                del counts[s[left]]      <span class="cm"># so len(counts) is the distinct count</span>
            left += 1
        best = max(best, right - left + 1)
    return best


def count_at_most(nums: list[int], k: int) -&gt; int:
    counts = {}
    left = 0
    total = 0
    for right, x in enumerate(nums):
        counts[x] = counts.get(x, 0) + 1
        while len(counts) &gt; k:
            counts[nums[left]] -= 1
            if counts[nums[left]] == 0:
                del counts[nums[left]]
            left += 1
        total += right - left + 1        <span class="cm"># all valid subarrays ENDING at right</span>
    return total


def subarraysWithKDistinct(nums: list[int], k: int) -&gt; int:
    <span class="cm"># "Exactly k" is not window-friendly, but "at most k" is:</span>
    return count_at_most(nums, k) - count_at_most(nums, k - 1)</pre>
    <p class="bf-note"><b>The trick:</b> <code>exactly(k) = atMost(k) − atMost(k − 1)</code>. The same subtraction solves any “exactly” count whose “at most” version is window-friendly (for example, LeetCode 1248 Count Number of Nice Subarrays). <b>Why <code>total += right − left + 1</code>:</b> every start between <code>left</code> and <code>right</code> gives a valid subarray ending at <code>right</code>.</p>
    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>subarraysWithKDistinct([1,2,1,2,3], 2)</code>: 7</div>
  </article>

  <article class="example">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example X.6</span><h3>Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array II</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 80</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Remove duplicates from a sorted array in place so each value appears <b>at most twice</b>. Return the new length. Generalizes Example 2.2.</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force — Count and Rebuild · O(N) time · O(N) space</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">def removeDuplicates_brute_force(nums: list[int], k: int = 2) -&gt; int:
    seen = {}
    kept = []
    for x in nums:
        if seen.get(x, 0) &lt; k:
            kept.append(x)
            seen[x] = seen.get(x, 0) + 1
    nums[:len(kept)] = kept
    return len(kept)</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Read &amp; Write with a k-Back Check · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code ">def removeDuplicates(nums: list[int], k: int = 2) -&gt; int:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 1: write pointer</span>
    write = 0

    <span class="cm"># Primitive 2 &amp; 4: read pointer scans every index</span>
    for read in range(len(nums)):
        <span class="cm"># The first k elements are always kept. After that, compare with the</span>
        <span class="cm"># element k slots BEHIND the write pointer (a "k-back" check).</span>
        if write &lt; k or nums[read] != nums[write - k]:
            <span class="cm"># Primitive 4: in-place overwrite at the write pointer</span>
            nums[write] = nums[read]
            write += 1
    return write</pre>
    <p class="bf-note"><code>k = 1</code> is Remove Duplicates (Example 2.2), <code>k = 2</code> is LeetCode 80, any <code>k</code> works. Comparing with <code>nums[write − k]</code> is enough because the array is sorted: if that slot equals the current value, all <code>k</code> slots in between hold it too.</p>
    <div class="subhead fc"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Remove Duplicates II — Compare k Slots Back</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 338" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Remove Duplicates II — Compare k Slots Back">
        <rect x="255" y="10" width="150" height="34" rx="9" fill="#0f2a4a"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">write = 0</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="210" y="72" width="240" height="44" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="91" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a">for read in range(n):</text>
        <text x="330" y="107" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="500" fill="#0f2a4a">scan every element</text>
        <path d="M330 116 L330 144" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <path d="M450 94 L500 94" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#2563eb">done</text>
        <rect x="500" y="76" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="98" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return write</text>
        <polygon points="330,144 458,178 330,212 202,178" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        <text x="330" y="174" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.7" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">write &lt; k  OR</text>
        <text x="330" y="190" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.7" font-weight="800" fill="#b45309">nums[read] ≠ nums[write−k] ?</text>
        <path d="M330 212 L330 240" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="339" y="230" text-anchor="start" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#2563eb">Yes</text>
        <path d="M458 178 L508 178" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="483" y="172" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="700" fill="#94a3b8">No</text>
        <rect x="508" y="160" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="573" y="182" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">skip</text>
        <rect x="227.2" y="240" width="205.6" height="46" rx="9" fill="#e8f0fb" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="259" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">nums[write] = nums[read]</text>
        <text x="330" y="275" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#0f2a4a" font-family="monospace">write++</text>
        <path d="M330 286 L330 316" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M573 196 L573 316" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M573 316 L10 316 L10 94 L210 94" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>[0,0,1,1,1,1,2,3,3]</code>: length 7 → [0,0,1,1,2,3,3]</div>
  </article>

  <article class="example">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example X.7</span><h3>Rotate Array</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 189</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Rotate an array to the right by <code>k</code> steps, in place.</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force — Extra Array · O(N) time · O(N) space</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">def rotate_brute_force(nums: list[int], k: int) -&gt; None:
    n = len(nums)
    if n == 0:
        return
    rotated = [0] * n
    for i in range(n):
        rotated[(i + k) % n] = nums[i]
    nums[:] = rotated</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Three Reversals · O(N) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code ">def rotate(nums: list[int], k: int) -&gt; None:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 1 + Guard: empty array, and k may exceed n</span>
    n = len(nums)
    if n == 0:
        return
    k %= n

    def reverse(l: int, r: int) -&gt; None:
        <span class="cm"># Pattern 1 + Primitive 3: converge and swap</span>
        while l &lt; r:
            nums[l], nums[r] = nums[r], nums[l]
            l += 1
            r -= 1

    reverse(0, n - 1)       <span class="cm"># whole array</span>
    reverse(0, k - 1)       <span class="cm"># first k elements</span>
    reverse(k, n - 1)       <span class="cm"># the rest</span></pre>
    <div class="viz-label">Reverse all → reverse first k → reverse the rest · <code>k = 3</code></div>
<div class="viz"><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">7</div><div class="idx">0</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">6</div><div class="idx">1</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">5</div><div class="idx">2</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">4</div><div class="idx">3</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">3</div><div class="idx">4</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">2</div><div class="idx">5</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">1</div><div class="idx">6</div></div></div>
<div class="viz"><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell g">5</div><div class="idx">0</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell g">6</div><div class="idx">1</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell g">7</div><div class="idx">2</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">4</div><div class="idx">3</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">3</div><div class="idx">4</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">2</div><div class="idx">5</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell i">1</div><div class="idx">6</div></div></div>
<div class="viz"><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell g">5</div><div class="idx">0</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell g">6</div><div class="idx">1</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell g">7</div><div class="idx">2</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell a">1</div><div class="idx">3</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell a">2</div><div class="idx">4</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell a">3</div><div class="idx">5</div></div><div class="col"><div class="pslot"></div><div class="cell a">4</div><div class="idx">6</div></div></div>
    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>[1,2,3,4,5,6,7], k = 3</code>: [5,6,7,1,2,3,4]</div>
  </article>

  <article class="example indigo">
    <div class="ex-head"><span class="ex-tag">Example X.8</span><h3>Subarray Sum Equals K</h3><span class="lc">LeetCode 560</span></div>
    <p class="ex-problem">Count the contiguous subarrays whose sum equals <code>k</code>. The array <b>may contain negative numbers</b>.</p>
    <div class="subhead bf"><span class="dot"></span> Brute Force — Every Subarray · O(N²) time · O(1) space</div>
<pre class="code bf-code">def subarraySum_brute_force(nums: list[int], k: int) -&gt; int:
    count = 0
    for i in range(len(nums)):
        total = 0
        for j in range(i, len(nums)):
            total += nums[j]
            if total == k:
                count += 1
    return count</pre>
    <div class="subhead opt"><span class="dot"></span> Optimal — Prefix Sum + Hash Map · O(N) time · O(N) space</div>
<pre class="code indigo-code">def subarraySum(nums: list[int], k: int) -&gt; int:
    <span class="cm"># Primitive 8: running prefix sum; seen[p] = how many earlier prefixes equal p</span>
    seen = {0: 1}               <span class="cm"># the empty prefix</span>
    running = 0
    count = 0

    for x in nums:
        running += x
        <span class="cm"># A subarray ending here sums to k  &lt;=&gt;  an earlier prefix equals running - k</span>
        count += seen.get(running - k, 0)
        seen[running] = seen.get(running, 0) + 1
    return count</pre>
    <p class="bf-note"><b>Why not a sliding window?</b> With negatives, growing the window can <i>lower</i> the sum, so “shrink when too big” is no longer valid. <b>The prefix trick:</b> <code>sum(i..j) = prefix[j+1] − prefix[i] = k</code>, so look for earlier prefixes equal to <code>running − k</code>. (Hash tables are formalized in Volume 3, Hash Lookup; this is a preview.)</p>
    <div class="subhead fc-indigo"><span class="dot"></span> Algorithm Flowchart</div>
    <div class="flowchart-wrap">
      <div class="flowchart-title">Subarray Sum Equals K — Prefix Sum + Hash Map</div>
      <svg class="flowchart-svg" viewBox="0 0 660 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Subarray Sum Equals K — Prefix Sum + Hash Map">
        <rect x="173.1" y="10" width="313.8" height="34" rx="9" fill="#4338ca"/>
        <text x="330" y="32" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12.5" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">seen = {0: 1}; running = 0; count = 0</text>
        <path d="M330 44 L330 72" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="210" y="72" width="240" height="44" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="91" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81">for x in nums:</text>
        <text x="330" y="107" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="500" fill="#312e81">extend the prefix</text>
        <path d="M330 116 L330 144" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <path d="M450 94 L500 94" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <text x="475" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#4338ca">done</text>
        <rect x="500" y="76" width="130" height="36" rx="9" fill="#d9f0dc" stroke="#7cc48a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="565" y="98" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" font-weight="800" fill="#166534">return count</text>
        <rect x="245" y="144" width="170" height="36" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="166" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">running += x</text>
        <path d="M330 180 L330 208" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="220.3" y="208" width="219.4" height="36" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="230" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">count += seen[running − k]</text>
        <path d="M330 244 L330 272" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
        <rect x="245" y="272" width="170" height="36" rx="9" fill="#e0e7ff" stroke="#a5b4fc" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <text x="330" y="294" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="800" fill="#312e81" font-family="monospace">seen[running] += 1</text>
        <path d="M330 308 L330 338" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M330 338 L10 338 L10 94 L210 94" fill="none" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5,4" marker-end="url(#ar)"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="result-pill">Result for <code>[1,2,3], k = 3</code>: 2</div>
  </article>

  <!-- CHEAT SHEET -->
  <div class="page-break"></div>
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Reference</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge">Cheat Sheet</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">All 7 patterns, mechanics, and complexity at a glance</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table class="matrix">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width:17%">Pattern</th>
        <th style="width:28%">Core Mechanics</th>
        <th style="width:31%">Target LeetCode Problems</th>
        <th style="width:24%">Time &amp; Space</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>P1 · Converging</strong></td>
        <td class="mono">left = 0, right = n-1<br>while left &lt; right:</td>
        <td>344 Reverse String · 167 Two Sum II<br>11 Container With Most Water · 15 3Sum<br>42 Trapping Rain Water<br>5 Longest Palindromic Substring <span class="practice">(outward)</span></td>
        <td><span class="tag-green">O(N)</span><br><span class="tag-blue">O(1)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>P2 · Read-Write</strong></td>
        <td class="mono">write = 0<br>for read in range(n):</td>
        <td>27 Remove Element<br>26 Remove Duplicates · 283 Move Zeroes<br>80 Remove Duplicates II · 75 Sort Colors<br>189 Rotate Array</td>
        <td><span class="tag-green">O(N)</span><br><span class="tag-blue">O(1)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>P3 · Backwards Write</strong></td>
        <td class="mono">i, j, write = m-1, n-1, m+n-1<br>write -= 1</td>
        <td>977 Squares of a Sorted Array<br>88 Merge Sorted Array</td>
        <td><span class="tag-green">O(N)</span><br><span class="tag-amber">O(1) or O(N)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>P4 · Sliding Window</strong></td>
        <td class="mono">for right in range(n):<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;expand → shrink</td>
        <td>643 Max Average Subarray I<br>3 Longest Substring · 209 Min Size Subarray<br>438 Find All Anagrams<br>424 Char Replacement · 904 / 992 K-Distinct</td>
        <td><span class="tag-green">O(N)</span><br><span class="tag-teal">O(1)–O(k)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>P5 · Two-Array Merge</strong></td>
        <td class="mono">i = j = 0<br>while i &lt; len1 and j &lt; len2:</td>
        <td>392 Is Subsequence<br>350 Intersection of Two Arrays II<br><span class="practice">Practice next: 986 Interval List Intersections</span></td>
        <td><span class="tag-green">O(N+M)</span><br><span class="tag-purple">O(1)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>P6 · Prefix Sum</strong></td>
        <td class="mono">prefix[i+1] = prefix[i] + nums[i]<br>query = prefix[r+1] − prefix[l]</td>
        <td>303 Range Sum Query<br>724 Find Pivot Index<br>238 Product of Array Except Self<br>560 Subarray Sum = K <span class="practice">(prefix + hash)</span></td>
        <td><span class="tag-green">O(N) build · O(1) query</span><br><span class="tag-indigo">O(N) or O(1)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>P7 · Kadane</strong></td>
        <td class="mono">here = max(nums[i], here + nums[i])<br>best = max(best, here)</td>
        <td>53 Maximum Subarray<br>152 Maximum Product Subarray<br><span class="practice">Practice next: 918 Max Sum Circular Subarray</span></td>
        <td><span class="tag-green">O(N)</span><br><span class="tag-purple">O(1)</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Guarded Skipping</strong><br><span style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:var(--rose)">cross-cutting</span></td>
        <td class="mono">while left &lt; right and skip_condition:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;left += 1</td>
        <td>15 3Sum · 125 Valid Palindrome</td>
        <td><span class="tag-green">O(N)</span><br><span class="tag-rose">O(1)</span></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:26px;">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Choosing Safely</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge badge-amber">When a Pattern Breaks</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">The signal that tells you to switch</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table class="matrix">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width:15%">Pattern</th>
        <th style="width:26%">Needs</th>
        <th style="width:27%">Breaks when…</th>
        <th style="width:32%">Switch to</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>P1 · Converging</strong></td><td>Sorted or symmetric data</td><td>Input is unsorted and you need pairs</td><td>Sort first (Vol 2) or hash lookup (Vol 3)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>P2 · Read-Write</strong></td><td>Keep/skip decided from nearby elements</td><td>The output must be <i>longer</i> than the input</td><td>Backwards Write (P3), e.g. 1089 Duplicate Zeros</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>P3 · Backwards Write</strong></td><td>Spare room at the end, or sorted inputs</td><td>No spare room, or inputs unsorted</td><td>Extra array, or sort first</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>P4 · Sliding Window</strong></td><td>Adding hurts, removing helps (monotone)</td><td>Negative numbers, or an “exactly k” condition</td><td>Prefix + hash (X.8) or atMost(k) − atMost(k−1) (X.5)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>P5 · Two-Array Merge</strong></td><td>Both arrays sorted</td><td>Either array is unsorted</td><td>Sort first, or a hash set (Vol 3)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>P6 · Prefix Sum</strong></td><td>Static array, invertible operation</td><td>Values change between queries, or you need min/max</td><td>Fenwick / segment tree (Vol 4), monotonic deque (Vol 3)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>P7 · Kadane</strong></td><td>Contiguous subarray, sum or product goal</td><td>Extra limits: max length, circular, k deletions</td><td>Prefix + deque (Vol 3), DP (Vol 6). Circular (918) = max(Kadane, total − min-Kadane)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="bf-note"><b>Two-pointer family:</b> P1–P5 and Guarded Skipping all move two indices; P4 and X.5 also carry window state. Outward expansion (X.2) and the three-pointer partition (X.1) are the two common variants.</p>

  <!-- BUGS -->
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Debugging</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge">7 Critical Bugs</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">And how to prevent them</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bug">
    <div class="bug-num">1</div>
    <div class="bug-body">
      <h5>Off-by-One Boundary Errors</h5>
      <p>Always initialize <code>right = len(nums) - 1</code>. Writing <code>right = len(nums)</code> causes an <code>IndexError</code> on the first iteration.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bug">
    <div class="bug-num">2</div>
    <div class="bug-body">
      <h5>Unbounded Skipping Loops</h5>
      <p>Inner skipping loops <b>must</b> prepend <code>left &lt; right</code>. Otherwise pointers run past valid indices and either crash or loop forever.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bug">
    <div class="bug-num">3</div>
    <div class="bug-body">
      <h5>Overwriting Before Reading</h5>
      <p>In Read-Write patterns, always evaluate <code>nums[read]</code> <b>before</b> executing <code>nums[write] = nums[read]</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bug">
    <div class="bug-num">4</div>
    <div class="bug-body">
      <h5>Modifying Array Size Inside For Loops</h5>
      <p>Avoid <code>nums.pop()</code> or <code>del nums[i]</code> during iteration. Use Read-Write pointers to overwrite in place and return a virtual length.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bug">
    <div class="bug-num">5</div>
    <div class="bug-body">
      <h5>Forgetting to Remove From Window State on Shrink</h5>
      <p>Sliding-window bugs come from a window state that drifts out of sync with <code>[left, right]</code>. Every element added on expand must be removed on shrink. <b>Primitive 7's symmetric add/remove pair is the fix.</b></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bug">
    <div class="bug-num">6</div>
    <div class="bug-body">
      <h5>Prefix Array Missing the Leading Zero</h5>
      <p>Build <code>prefix = [0] * (n + 1)</code>, not <code>[0] * n</code>. Without the leading <code>prefix[0] = 0</code>, the query <code>sumRange(0, r)</code> has no clean left boundary and you'll special-case every <code>left == 0</code> call. The extra slot eliminates the entire class of edge-case bugs.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bug">
    <div class="bug-num">7</div>
    <div class="bug-body">
      <h5>Kadane Initialized to 0 Instead of nums[0]</h5>
      <p>On an all-negative array, initializing <code>best = 0</code> returns 0 instead of the largest (least negative) element. Initialize both <code>best</code> and <code>here</code> to <code>nums[0]</code>. For the product variant, also track <code>min_ending_here</code> — a negative times a negative can become the new maximum.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- PATTERN TEMPLATES -->
  <div class="page-break"></div>
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-kicker"><span class="tri">▶</span> Practice</div>
    <div class="sec-title-row">
