  <p class="tpl-intro">Cover the solutions above and complete each skeleton. Every blank (<code>____</code>) is a decision the pattern forces you to make.</p>
  <div class="tpl-grid">
    <div class="tpl"><div class="tpl-h">P1 · Converging</div><pre class="code ">left, right = 0, len(nums) - 1
while left &lt; right:
    total = ____
    if total &lt; ____:   left += 1
    elif total &gt; ____: right -= 1
    else:              ____</pre></div>
    <div class="tpl"><div class="tpl-h">P2 · Read-Write</div><pre class="code ">write = 0
for read in range(len(nums)):
    if ____:
        nums[write] = nums[read]
        write += 1
return write</pre></div>
    <div class="tpl"><div class="tpl-h">P3 · Backwards Write</div><pre class="code amber-code">res = [0] * n
left, right, write = 0, n-1, n-1
while left &lt;= right:
    if ____:
        res[write] = ____; left += 1
    else:
        res[write] = ____; right -= 1
    write -= 1</pre></div>
    <div class="tpl"><div class="tpl-h">P4 · Sliding Window</div><pre class="code teal-code">left = 0
for right in range(len(nums)):
    # expand: add nums[right]
    while ____:      # window invalid?
        # shrink: remove nums[left]
        left += 1
    best = ____(best, right-left+1)</pre></div>
    <div class="tpl"><div class="tpl-h">P5 · Two-Array Merge</div><pre class="code purple-code">i = j = 0
while i &lt; len(a) and j &lt; len(b):
    if a[i] == b[j]:
        ____; i += 1; j += 1
    elif a[i] &lt; b[j]: i += 1
    else:             j += 1</pre></div>
    <div class="tpl"><div class="tpl-h">P6 · Prefix Sum</div><pre class="code indigo-code">prefix = [0] * (n + 1)
for i in range(n):
    prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] + ____
range_sum = prefix[____] - prefix[____]</pre></div>
    <div class="tpl"><div class="tpl-h">P7 · Kadane</div><pre class="code purple-code">here = best = nums[0]
for x in nums[1:]:
    here = max(____, here + x)
    best = max(best, ____)
return best</pre></div>
    <div class="tpl"><div class="tpl-h">Guarded Skipping</div><pre class="code rose-code">while left &lt; right and ____:
    left += 1
while left &lt; right and ____:
    right -= 1</pre></div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec-head" style="margin-top:22px;">
    <div class="sec-title-row">
      <span class="badge badge-rose">Edge-Case Checklist</span>
      <span class="sec-sub">Run through this before you submit</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="chk-grid"><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Empty input and single-element input</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>All elements equal; many duplicates</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Negatives and zeros (windows break; products zero out)</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Already sorted and reverse sorted</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span><code>k = 0</code>, <code>k ≥ n</code>, or <code>k &gt; n</code> (rotate: <code>k %= n</code>)</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Loop bound: <code>&lt;</code> or <code>&lt;=</code> — is the last element processed?</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Inner skipping loops start with <code>left &lt; right</code></div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Mutated in place or returned a new list?</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>After a swap, does the swapped-in value still need checking?</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Unicode, case, non-alphanumeric characters (strings)</div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Java / C++: <code>mid = lo + (hi − lo) / 2</code>; sums in <code>long</code></div><div class="chk-item"><span class="cb"></span>Does a stale value (like <code>max_freq</code>) stay safe? State why.</div></div>

