  <p style="font-size:13.5px;color:#475569;margin-bottom:18px;">
    Each volume covers one data-structure family. Within a volume you learn the primitives that structure needs, then the patterns built on those primitives. Base primitives (1–8) carry forward; structure primitives (numbered per-volume) stay local.
  </p>

